        "description": "Nexus Water Group, Inc. is a regulated water and wastewater utility platform formed when the U.S. regulated operations of Corix Infrastructure combined with SouthWest Water Company on April 1, 2024. The business operates locally branded systems across the United States and Canada and serves more than 1.3 million people. BCI owns 50.0% through its Infrastructure & Renewable Resources program. The other 50% is held through SWMAC Holdco, producing indirect platform interests of 37.5% for J.P. Morgan Asset Management's Infrastructure Investments Fund and 12.5% for a Munich Re vehicle managed by MEAG. Nexus completed the sale of systems in eight states to American Water on June 1, 2026, while its announced Nevada and Oregon asset sale remained pending; neither transaction is a sponsor sale or platform exit.",
